# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — WIDTH-BOUNDARY axis.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_width_boundary_axis`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Every row is SUFFIX-FREE (a vardecl, so nothing is emitted after the closing
# bracket on that line) and uses FLAT SCALAR elements, so the asserted column is
# exactly the packer's arithmetic with no pre-render or caller-suffix noise.
#
# Cells sampled (Core #12 — this file samples the `width boundary` axis ONLY;
# `MAX_WIDTH` is 120):
#   wb119   flat width 119  <  budget  => one line
#   wb120   flat width 120  == budget  => one line (the boundary is INCLUSIVE)
#   wb121   flat width 121  >  budget  => the last element that does not fit
#                                         breaks to the continuation indent
#   wbline  LINE-INITIAL list: the statement IS the list, so the Doc render
#           starts with the indentation still unwritten. Its true flat width is
#           124; measured from a raw `col` of 0 it looks like 120 and would be
#           emitted flat, four columns over budget. This row pins
#           `Emitter::current_col()`.
#
# RED source per row: wb119 / wb120 / wb121 are TRUE pre-fix REDs — at
# MAX_WIDTH=100 all three break, and one-per-line at that. wbline is a TRUE
# pre-fix RED for a second, independent reason: revert `write_doc` to pass
# `self.emitter.col` and it is emitted as a single 124-column line.
void wb():
    Vector[int] wb119 = [11111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 121212, 131313]
    Vector[int] wb120 = [111111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 121212, 131313]
    Vector[int] wb121 = [1111111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 121212, 131313]

void wbline():
    [111111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 121212, 131313, 141414, 151515, 161616]
